IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fhog-core`

-- First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (NT) -- the first home buyer's questions.
--
-- SEAT: the first home buyer applying for the grant, with their spouse or de facto partner (who may apply with them, and
-- whose history counts either way: ss 6, 10, 11, 12A). "Am I eligible? Is my contract an eligible transaction? How much
-- is my grant? By when must I apply and move in, and for how long? When must I repay?" Every question is phrased as the
-- buyer would ask it, on facts the buyer could state. The rules are in fhog-core.l4; this module builds the core's
-- records from plain answers and restates no rule.
--
-- The same answers are asked in the same order in every question that needs them, so the form can ask them once:
-- the transaction (what it is, the contract date, the foundations date, then the home and price facts), completion, my
-- own facts, then my spouse's or de facto partner's, then the other owners, then the day asked about.
--
-- The NT levies no land tax, so a first home buyer here meets only this grant and stamp duty (whose home concessions are
-- in the stamp-duty-act-1978 encoding).
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `First home owner grant -- the buyer's questions`

§§ `Building the core's records from my answers`

GIVEN `kind`                         IS A `Transaction kind`
      `contract date`                IS A DATE
      `foundations date`             IS A DATE
      `in the Territory`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `lawfully usable`              IS A BOOLEAN
      `considered suitable`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `owner of the land`            IS A BOOLEAN
      `lived in or sold before`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `renovated new premises`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `lived in since renovation`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `declared new`                 IS A BOOLEAN
      `replacement`                  IS A BOOLEAN
      `old option`                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `price`                        IS A NUMBER
      `home value`                   IS A NUMBER
      `land value`                   IS A NUMBER
      `urban`                        IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Transaction`
`my transaction from my answers` MEANS
    `Transaction` WITH
        `kind`                                                                                            IS `kind`
        `the date the contract was made`                                                                  IS `contract date`
        `the date laying the foundations commenced`                                                       IS `foundations date`
        `the home is in the Territory`                                                                    IS `in the Territory`
        `the building is a home`                                                                          IS `the building is a home (s 4)` `lawfully usable` `considered suitable`
        `new home facts`                                                                                  IS `my new home facts` `lived in or sold before` `renovated new premises` `lived in since renovation` `declared new`
        `the applicant is, or on completion will be, an owner of the land`                                IS `owner of the land`
        `it replaces an earlier contract made, or is made under an option or right granted, before 1 October 2024` IS `replacement`
        `an option or right granted before 1 July 2000 applies and the Commissioner has not declared it eligible`  IS `old option`
        `the consideration`                                                                               IS `price`
        `the unencumbered value of the home`                                                              IS `home value`
        `the unencumbered value of the relevant interest in the land`                                     IS `land value`
        `the land is wholly within the urban area`                                                        IS `urban`

GIVEN `lived in or sold before`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `renovated new premises`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `lived in since renovation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `declared new`              IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `New home facts`
`my new home facts` MEANS
    `New home facts` WITH
        `the home has been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence`                    IS `lived in or sold before`
        `its sale is a taxable supply of new residential premises under s 40-75(1)(b) of the GST Act` IS `renovated new premises`
        `it has been occupied or sold as a place of residence since being renovated`               IS `lived in since renovation`
        `the Commissioner has declared it a new home under s 4A(2)`                                IS `declared new`

GIVEN `possession date`     IS A DATE
      `registered title`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `registration date`   IS A DATE
      `ready date`          IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Completion facts`
`my completion facts` MEANS
    `Completion facts` WITH
        `the date the purchaser becomes entitled to possession of the home`                       IS `possession date`
        `the purchaser is to obtain a registered title to the land`                               IS `registered title`
        `the date the necessary steps to obtain registration of the purchaser's title are taken`  IS `registration date`
        `the date the building is ready for occupation as a place of residence`                   IS `ready date`

GIVEN `earlier grant`        IS AN `Earlier grant`
      `could have applied`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `unpaid discount duty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `earlier property`     IS AN `Earlier residential property`
GIVETH A `History`
`the history from the answers` MEANS
    `History` WITH
        `earlier grant`                                                                                  IS `earlier grant`
        `could have successfully applied for a grant on an earlier transaction`                         IS `could have applied`
        `received the first home owner discount on an earlier conveyance and the duty forgone has not been paid` IS `unpaid discount duty`
        `earlier residential property`                                                                   IS `earlier property`

-- One applicant from the answers about them, with the history of their spouse or de facto partner. `is a natural person`
-- is TRUE: the seat is an individual (s 8(1)(a) is met by everyone who can ask these questions).
GIVEN `age`                  IS A NUMBER
      `age exemption`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `status`               IS A `Citizenship or visa`
      `own history`          IS A `History`
      `has a partner`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `partner's history`    IS A `History`
      `will live there`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `residence exemption`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Applicant`
`an applicant from the answers` MEANS
    `Applicant` WITH
        `is a natural person`                                                               IS TRUE
        `age at the commencement date`                                                      IS `age`
        `the Commissioner has exempted the applicant from the age requirement under s 8(2)` IS `age exemption`
        `citizenship or visa at the time of the application`                                IS `status`
        `own history`                                                                       IS `own history`
        `has a spouse or de facto partner`                                                  IS `has a partner`
        `history of the spouse or de facto partner`                                         IS `partner's history`
        `will occupy the home as the principal place of residence as s 12(2) requires`      IS `will live there`
        `the Commissioner has exempted the applicant from the residence requirement under s 12(3)(b)` IS `residence exemption`

-- The applicants: me, and my spouse or de facto partner if they apply with me.
GIVEN `my age`                         IS A NUMBER
      `my age exemption`               IS A BOOLEAN
      `my status`                      IS A `Citizenship or visa`
      `my earlier grant`               IS AN `Earlier grant`
      `I could have applied`           IS A BOOLEAN
      `my unpaid discount duty`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `my earlier property`            IS AN `Earlier residential property`
      `I will live there`              IS A BOOLEAN
      `my residence exemption`         IS A BOOLEAN
      `relationship`                   IS A `Relationship at the commencement date`
      `living apart for good`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `partner applying`               IS A BOOLEAN
      `partner's age`                  IS A NUMBER
      `partner's age exemption`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `partner's status`               IS A `Citizenship or visa`
      `partner's earlier grant`        IS AN `Earlier grant`
      `partner could have applied`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `partner's unpaid discount duty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `partner's earlier property`     IS AN `Earlier residential property`
      `partner will live there`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `partner's residence exemption`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Applicant`
`the applicants from my answers` MEANS
    IF `partner applying`
    THEN LIST `me`, `my partner`
    ELSE LIST `me`
    WHERE
        `the partner counts` MEANS `the applicant has a spouse or de facto partner (s 6)` `relationship` `living apart for good`
        `my history` MEANS `the history from the answers` `my earlier grant` `I could have applied` `my unpaid discount duty` `my earlier property`
        `the partner's history` MEANS `the history from the answers` `partner's earlier grant` `partner could have applied` `partner's unpaid discount duty` `partner's earlier property`
        `me` MEANS `an applicant from the answers` `my age` `my age exemption` `my status` `my history` `the partner counts` `the partner's history` `I will live there` `my residence exemption`
        `my partner` MEANS `an applicant from the answers` `partner's age` `partner's age exemption` `partner's status` `the partner's history` `the partner counts` `my history` `partner will live there` `partner's residence exemption`

§§ `s 6 -- my spouse or de facto partner`

@export Does my husband, wife or de facto partner count as my spouse or de facto partner for the NT first home owner grant (s 6)? Their past grants and homes then count against me.
GIVEN `my relationship on the commencement date` IS A `Relationship at the commencement date` @desc Your relationship on the commencement date (the day your contract was made, or for an owner build the day laying the foundations began). One of: no spouse or de facto partner, married, a de facto partner
      `the Commissioner is satisfied we live apart for good` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Married applicants only: whether the Commissioner is satisfied that you and your husband or wife are not living together and you have no intention of living together again
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my spouse or de facto partner count for the grant` IS
    `the applicant has a spouse or de facto partner (s 6)` `my relationship on the commencement date` `the Commissioner is satisfied we live apart for good`

§§ `ss 7(1)(a), 8-12A -- am I eligible`

@export Am I (and my spouse or de facto partner, if applying with me) eligible for the NT first home owner grant under the eligibility criteria (ss 7(1)(a), 8-12A)? Says which criterion fails, if one does.
GIVEN `what my transaction is` IS A `Transaction kind` @desc What the grant is sought for. One of: a contract for the purchase of a home; a comprehensive home building contract (a builder builds the whole home for you); the building of a home by an owner builder; the purchase of a building to be placed on land in which the purchaser has a relevant interest (a transportable or relocated home)
      `the date my contract was made` IS A DATE @desc The date your purchase or building contract was made, or the date of the contract to buy a building you will move onto your land (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date laying the foundations began` IS A DATE @desc Owner builders only: the date laying the foundations for the home began, or another date the Commissioner has fixed as appropriate (YYYY-MM-DD; for any other transaction give the contract date again)
      `my age on the commencement date` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years on the commencement date (the contract date, or for an owner build the foundations date)
      `the Commissioner has exempted me from the age requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has exempted you from having to be 18 (s 8(2): only if satisfied you will live in the home and the application does not get around the Act)
      `my citizenship or visa when I apply` IS A `Citizenship or visa` @desc Your status on the day you apply. One of: an Australian citizen; the holder of a permanent visa; a New Zealand citizen who holds a special category visa; none of these
      `my earlier grant` IS AN `Earlier grant` @desc Whether you were paid a first home owner grant before, in the NT or any other State or Territory. One of: no grant was paid on an earlier application; a grant was paid on an earlier application and has not been paid back with any penalty and interest; a grant was paid on an earlier application and was paid back with any penalty and interest; a grant was paid on an earlier application for a home used as a residence, on a transaction over the threshold amount
      `I could have got a grant before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you could have successfully applied for a first home owner grant (in any State or Territory) for an earlier purchase or build you were a party to, but did not, or could have if you had then been a citizen or permanent resident
      `I have unpaid duty from a first home owner discount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you got the NT stamp duty first home owner discount (Stamp Duty Act s 89AA) on an earlier purchase and the duty it saved has not been paid
      `my earlier residential property` IS AN `Earlier residential property` @desc Your past ownership of homes anywhere in Australia, the first that applies. One of: never held a relevant interest in residential property in Australia; held a relevant interest in residential property in Australia before 1 July 2000; held one from 1 July 2000, before the commencement date, in property used as a residence of the person or their spouse or de facto partner; held one from 1 July 2000 only in property that was the subject of an earlier application whose grant was repaid, or was not paid for want of an age exemption; held one from 1 July 2000 only in property that neither the person nor their spouse or de facto partner used as a residence
      `I will live in the home as required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you will live in the home as your principal place of residence, moving in within 12 months of completion and staying for the required period (12 months for contracts from 1 Oct 2024 to before 1 Oct 2027, otherwise 6 months)
      `the Commissioner has exempted me from living in the home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has exempted you from the residence requirement for special reasons (s 12(3)(b))
      `my relationship on the commencement date` IS A `Relationship at the commencement date` @desc Your relationship on the commencement date. One of: no spouse or de facto partner, married, a de facto partner
      `the Commissioner is satisfied we live apart for good` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Married applicants only: whether the Commissioner is satisfied that you and your husband or wife are not living together and have no intention of living together again
      `my spouse or de facto partner is applying with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse or de facto partner is a joint applicant (they must be if they will own any part of the home, s 15)
      `my partner's age on the commencement date` IS A NUMBER @desc Your spouse's or de facto partner's age in whole years on the commencement date (only if applying with you)
      `the Commissioner has exempted my partner from the age requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has exempted your spouse or de facto partner from having to be 18 (only if applying with you)
      `my partner's citizenship or visa when we apply` IS A `Citizenship or visa` @desc Your spouse's or de facto partner's status on the day you apply (only if applying with you). One of: an Australian citizen; the holder of a permanent visa; a New Zealand citizen who holds a special category visa; none of these
      `my partner's earlier grant` IS AN `Earlier grant` @desc Whether your spouse or de facto partner was paid a first home owner grant before, anywhere in Australia (same choices as for you)
      `my partner could have got a grant before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse or de facto partner could have successfully applied for a first home owner grant for an earlier purchase or build they were a party to
      `my partner has unpaid duty from a first home owner discount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse or de facto partner got the NT first home owner duty discount on an earlier purchase and the duty it saved has not been paid
      `my partner's earlier residential property` IS AN `Earlier residential property` @desc Your spouse's or de facto partner's past ownership of homes anywhere in Australia (same choices as for you)
      `my partner will live in the home as required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse or de facto partner will live in the home as their principal place of residence as required (only if applying with you)
      `the Commissioner has exempted my partner from living in the home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has exempted your spouse or de facto partner from the residence requirement (only if applying with you)
      `someone besides me and my partner is applying with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anyone other than you and your spouse or de facto partner (a sibling, parent or friend who will co-own the home) is on the application; their facts are not asked here
GIVETH AN `Eligibility answer`
DECIDE `Am I eligible for the first home owner grant` IS
    IF `someone besides me and my partner is applying with me`
    THEN `eligibility not covered` `an applicant whose facts are not given`
    ELSE `the eligibility of the applicants (ss 7(1)(a), 8-12A)` `commencement`
            (`the applicants from my answers` `my age on the commencement date` `the Commissioner has exempted me from the age requirement` `my citizenship or visa when I apply` `my earlier grant` `I could have got a grant before` `I have unpaid duty from a first home owner discount` `my earlier residential property` `I will live in the home as required` `the Commissioner has exempted me from living in the home` `my relationship on the commencement date` `the Commissioner is satisfied we live apart for good` `my spouse or de facto partner is applying with me` `my partner's age on the commencement date` `the Commissioner has exempted my partner from the age requirement` `my partner's citizenship or visa when we apply` `my partner's earlier grant` `my partner could have got a grant before` `my partner has unpaid duty from a first home owner discount` `my partner's earlier residential property` `my partner will live in the home as required` `the Commissioner has exempted my partner from living in the home`)
    WHERE
        -- Only the kind and the two dates are read to find the commencement date; the other fields are placeholders.
        `commencement` MEANS `the commencement date (s 13(5))` (`my transaction from my answers` `what my transaction is` `the date my contract was made` `the date laying the foundations began` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 FALSE)

§§ `ss 4, 4A, 5, 13, 13AA, regs r 3 -- is my contract an eligible transaction`

@export Is my home a "new home" for the NT first home owner grant (s 4A)?
GIVEN `what my transaction is` IS A `Transaction kind` @desc What the grant is sought for. One of: a contract for the purchase of a home; a comprehensive home building contract; the building of a home by an owner builder; the purchase of a building to be placed on land in which the purchaser has a relevant interest
      `the home has been lived in or sold as a residence before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home has ever been occupied or sold as a place of residence, including as a hotel room, serviced apartment or workers accommodation (answer no for a home being built for you)
      `my purchase is a taxable sale of substantially renovated new residential premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your purchase is, under the GST Act, a taxable supply of new residential premises created by substantial renovation (s 40-75(1)(b)); your contract or the seller can tell you
      `the home has been lived in or sold as a residence since it was renovated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home has been occupied or sold as a place of residence since that substantial renovation
      `the Commissioner has declared my home a new home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has declared the home a new home for your transaction (s 4A(2), for a home that would be new but for an earlier sale)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my home a new home` IS
    `the home is a new home (s 4A)` `what my transaction is` (`my new home facts` `the home has been lived in or sold as a residence before` `my purchase is a taxable sale of substantially renovated new residential premises` `the home has been lived in or sold as a residence since it was renovated` `the Commissioner has declared my home a new home`)

@export Do I have (or on completion will I have) a "relevant interest" in the land, so that I count as its owner for the NT first home owner grant (s 5, Regulations r 3)?
GIVEN `my interest in the land` IS AN `Interest in land` @desc The interest you have or will have in the land. One of: an estate in fee simple (freehold title); a life estate approved by the Commissioner; a perpetual lease granted by the Commonwealth or the Territory; a lease granted by the Commonwealth or the Territory that may be converted into an estate in fee simple; an interest as purchaser of an estate in fee simple by instalments; a licence or right of occupancy granted by the Commonwealth or the Territory that the Commissioner considers gives reasonable security of tenure; an interest as lessee or sublessee under a registered lease granted by the Commonwealth or the Territory; an interest as lessee or sublessee under a registered lease or sublease granted under s 19 or 19A of the Aboriginal Land Rights (Northern Territory) Act 1976; none of these interests
      `the term of my lease in years` IS A NUMBER @desc For a registered Crown lease or a lease or sublease under s 19 or 19A of the Aboriginal Land Rights (Northern Territory) Act 1976: its term in years (otherwise 0)
      `I can occupy the land within 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have, or will have within 12 months (or a longer period the Commissioner allows), a right to immediate occupation of the land
      `I hold the interest on trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold the interest subject to a trust (for example as trustee for someone else)
      `my interest is only equitable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your interest is only an equitable one (not a legal title in your name)
      `a guardian holds it in trust for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a guardian holds the interest in trust for you because you are under a legal disability
      `I am the lessor of the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the lessor or sublessor (the landlord) under one of the leases listed above
      `I am building on land someone else owns` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a building contract for, or have begun building or having built, a home on land owned by someone else
      `that land is farming land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that land is used solely or principally for farming purposes (as the Stamp Duty Act s 4(1) uses the term)
      `the owner of that land` IS AN `Owner of the land` @desc Who owns the land you are building on. One of: a spouse or de facto partner of the person; a parent of the person, or of the person's spouse or de facto partner; a grandparent of the person, or of the person's spouse or de facto partner; a sibling of the person, or of the person's spouse or de facto partner; a child of the person, including an adopted child or a stepchild; a grandchild of the person; a spouse or de facto partner of a sibling, child or grandchild in this list; someone who is not a relative of the person
      `the owner has given me permission to live in the home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner of that land has given you permission to occupy the home when it is completed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have a relevant interest in the land` IS
    `the person has a relevant interest in the land (s 5, regs r 3)` `my interest` `my building`
    WHERE
        `my interest` MEANS
            `Interest facts` WITH
                `the interest` IS `my interest in the land`
                `the term of the lease in years` IS `the term of my lease in years`
                `the holder has, or will have within 12 months or a longer period the Commissioner allows, a right to immediate occupation of the land` IS `I can occupy the land within 12 months`
                `the holder holds it subject to a trust` IS `I hold the interest on trust`
                `it is an equitable interest` IS `my interest is only equitable`
                `a guardian holds it in trust for the holder, a person under a legal disability` IS `a guardian holds it in trust for me`
                `the holder is the lessor or sublessor under a lease or sublease mentioned in s 5(2)` IS `I am the lessor of the land`
        `my building` MEANS
            `Building on another's land` WITH
                `the person has entered into a comprehensive home building contract, or begun building a home or having one built, on the land` IS `I am building on land someone else owns`
                `the land is used solely or principally for farming purposes` IS `that land is farming land`
                `the owner of the land` IS `the owner of that land`
                `the owner of the land has given permission for the person to occupy the home when it is completed` IS `the owner has given me permission to live in the home`

@export What is the commencement date of my transaction for the NT first home owner grant (s 13(5))? It fixes which rules and amounts apply.
GIVEN `what my transaction is` IS A `Transaction kind` @desc What the grant is sought for. One of: a contract for the purchase of a home; a comprehensive home building contract; the building of a home by an owner builder; the purchase of a building to be placed on land in which the purchaser has a relevant interest
      `the date my contract was made` IS A DATE @desc The date your purchase or building contract was made, or the date of the contract to buy a building you will move onto your land (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date laying the foundations began` IS A DATE @desc Owner builders only: the date laying the foundations began, or another date the Commissioner has fixed (YYYY-MM-DD; otherwise give the contract date again)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the commencement date of my transaction` IS
    -- Only the kind and the two dates are read; the other fields are placeholders.
    `the commencement date (s 13(5))` (`my transaction from my answers` `what my transaction is` `the date my contract was made` `the date laying the foundations began` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 FALSE)

@export When is my transaction "completed" for the NT first home owner grant (s 13(6))? The grant is payable, and the deadlines to apply and move in run, from completion.
GIVEN `what my transaction is` IS A `Transaction kind` @desc What the grant is sought for. One of: a contract for the purchase of a home; a comprehensive home building contract; the building of a home by an owner builder; the purchase of a building to be placed on land in which the purchaser has a relevant interest
      `the date I become entitled to possession` IS A DATE @desc Purchases: the date you become entitled to possession of the home under the contract (usually settlement) (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `I am to get a registered title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Purchases: whether you are to obtain a registered title to the land
      `the date the steps to register my title are taken` IS A DATE @desc Purchases with a registered title: the date the necessary steps to register your title are taken (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date the home is ready to live in` IS A DATE @desc Building contracts, owner builds and relocated buildings: the date the building is ready for occupation as a place of residence on your land (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `When is my transaction completed` IS
    `the completion date (s 13(6))` `what my transaction is` (`my completion facts` `the date I become entitled to possession` `I am to get a registered title` `the date the steps to register my title are taken` `the date the home is ready to live in`)

@export Is my contract or build an "eligible transaction" for the NT first home owner grant (ss 13, 13AA)? Says why not, if it is not.
GIVEN `what my transaction is` IS A `Transaction kind` @desc What the grant is sought for. One of: a contract for the purchase of a home; a comprehensive home building contract (a builder builds the whole home for you); the building of a home by an owner builder; the purchase of a building to be placed on land in which the purchaser has a relevant interest (a transportable or relocated home)
      `the date my contract was made` IS A DATE @desc The date your purchase or building contract was made, or the date of the contract to buy a building you will move onto your land (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date laying the foundations began` IS A DATE @desc Owner builders only: the date laying the foundations for the home began, or another date the Commissioner has fixed as appropriate (YYYY-MM-DD; for any other transaction give the contract date again)
      `the home is in the Northern Territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home is (or will be) in the Northern Territory
      `the building is fixed to land and may lawfully be lived in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the building is affixed to land and may lawfully be used as a place of residence
      `the Commissioner considers the building suitable to live in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner considers it a suitable building for use as a place of residence (s 4(b)); answer yes unless told otherwise
      `I am or will be an owner of the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have, or on completion will have, a relevant interest in the land the home is on (see the relevant interest question: usually freehold title, a convertible Crown lease, or a registered lease of 15 years or more)
      `the home has been lived in or sold as a residence before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home has ever been occupied or sold as a place of residence, including as a hotel room, serviced apartment or workers accommodation (answer no for a home being built for you)
      `my purchase is a taxable sale of substantially renovated new residential premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your purchase is, under the GST Act, a taxable supply of new residential premises created by substantial renovation (s 40-75(1)(b))
      `the home has been lived in or sold as a residence since it was renovated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home has been occupied or sold as a place of residence since that substantial renovation
      `the Commissioner has declared my home a new home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has declared the home a new home for your transaction (s 4A(2))
      `my contract replaces one made, or uses an option granted, before 1 October 2024` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your contract replaces an earlier contract for the same or a substantially similar home made before 1 October 2024, or is made under an option or right granted before then (Part 5; not covered here)
      `my contract was made under an option granted before 1 July 2000` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an option or right granted before 1 July 2000 applies to the contract and the Commissioner has not declared it an eligible transaction (s 13AA(1)(a)): for a purchase, you had an option to buy the home, or the seller an option to require you to buy it; for a building contract, either party had a right or option to require the other to enter into it. Almost always no. A contract made in exercise of such an option is also one made under an option granted before 1 October 2024, so answer yes to that question too
      `the price, including GST` IS A NUMBER @desc The consideration in dollars, including GST: for a purchase the price; for a building contract the total price of the building work; for an owner build what the work actually cost you, not counting your own labour; leave out rent under a lease
      `the unencumbered value of the home` IS A NUMBER @desc Only for transactions that commenced before 1 January 2015: the full value of the home in dollars, ignoring mortgages and other encumbrances, including GST (otherwise 0)
      `the unencumbered value of my interest in the land` IS A NUMBER @desc Only for transactions that commenced before 1 January 2015: the full value of your interest in the land in dollars, ignoring encumbrances, including GST (otherwise 0)
      `the land is wholly within the Darwin urban area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is wholly within the urban area: the Municipalities of Darwin, Palmerston and Litchfield, the Shire of Wagait, Prescribed Area A under the NT Rates Regulations, or the Darwin Waterfront Precinct (matters only to contracts from 4 Dec 2012 to before 1 Jan 2015)
GIVETH A `Transaction answer`
DECIDE `Is my transaction an eligible transaction` IS
    `whether the transaction is an eligible transaction (ss 13, 13AA)`
        (`my transaction from my answers` `what my transaction is` `the date my contract was made` `the date laying the foundations began` `the home is in the Northern Territory` `the building is fixed to land and may lawfully be lived in` `the Commissioner considers the building suitable to live in` `I am or will be an owner of the land` `the home has been lived in or sold as a residence before` `my purchase is a taxable sale of substantially renovated new residential premises` `the home has been lived in or sold as a residence since it was renovated` `the Commissioner has declared my home a new home` `my contract replaces one made, or uses an option granted, before 1 October 2024` `my contract was made under an option granted before 1 July 2000` `the price, including GST` `the unencumbered value of the home` `the unencumbered value of my interest in the land` `the land is wholly within the Darwin urban area`)

§§ `s 18 -- how much is my grant`

@export How much is my NT first home owner grant, if it is payable (s 18)? The lesser of the price and the amount for the commencement date: $50,000 for a new home from 1 Oct 2024 to before 1 Oct 2027, $10,000 after.
GIVEN `what my transaction is` IS A `Transaction kind` @desc What the grant is sought for. One of: a contract for the purchase of a home; a comprehensive home building contract; the building of a home by an owner builder; the purchase of a building to be placed on land in which the purchaser has a relevant interest
      `the date my contract was made` IS A DATE @desc The date your purchase or building contract was made, or the date of the contract to buy a building you will move onto your land (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date laying the foundations began` IS A DATE @desc Owner builders only: the date laying the foundations began, or another date the Commissioner has fixed (YYYY-MM-DD; otherwise give the contract date again)
      `the home has been lived in or sold as a residence before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home has ever been occupied or sold as a place of residence, including as a hotel room, serviced apartment or workers accommodation (answer no for a home being built for you)
      `my purchase is a taxable sale of substantially renovated new residential premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your purchase is, under the GST Act, a taxable supply of new residential premises created by substantial renovation (s 40-75(1)(b))
      `the home has been lived in or sold as a residence since it was renovated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home has been occupied or sold as a place of residence since that substantial renovation
      `the Commissioner has declared my home a new home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has declared the home a new home for your transaction (s 4A(2))
      `my contract replaces one made, or uses an option granted, before 1 October 2024` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your contract replaces an earlier contract made before 1 October 2024, or is made under an option or right granted before then (not covered here)
      `the price, including GST` IS A NUMBER @desc The consideration actually paid, in dollars, including GST: the price, the total price of the building work, or for an owner build what the work actually cost (not your own labour)
      `the land is wholly within the Darwin urban area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is wholly within the urban area (Darwin, Palmerston, Litchfield, Wagait, Prescribed Area A, the Darwin Waterfront Precinct); matters only from 4 Dec 2012 to before 1 Jan 2015
GIVETH AN `Amount answer`
DECIDE `How much is my first home owner grant` IS
    -- Fields s 18 does not read (the Territory, s 4, ownership, the 2000 option, unencumbered values) are placeholders.
    `the amount of the grant (s 18)`
        (`my transaction from my answers` `what my transaction is` `the date my contract was made` `the date laying the foundations began` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `the home has been lived in or sold as a residence before` `my purchase is a taxable sale of substantially renovated new residential premises` `the home has been lived in or sold as a residence since it was renovated` `the Commissioner has declared my home a new home` `my contract replaces one made, or uses an option granted, before 1 October 2024` FALSE `the price, including GST` 0 0 `the land is wholly within the Darwin urban area`)

§§ `ss 7, 15, 17 -- is the grant payable to me`

@export Must this other owner of the home join in my application for the NT first home owner grant (s 15, Regulations r 4)?
GIVEN `this person will own the home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is, or on completion will be, an owner of the home (has a relevant interest in the land it is on)
      `this person is the Chief Executive Officer (Housing)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is the Chief Executive Officer (Housing), the NT housing body corporate (for example under a shared ownership scheme)
      `this person owns the land I build on under Regulations r 3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is the owner of farming land or a relative's land on which you are building with their permission, so that your relevant interest comes only from Regulations r 3
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must this owner join in my application` IS
    `the person is an interested person who must be an applicant (s 15, regs r 4)` `this person will own the home` `this person is the Chief Executive Officer (Housing)` `this person owns the land I build on under Regulations r 3`

@export Is the NT first home owner grant payable to me (and my spouse or de facto partner, if applying with me), and how much (ss 7, 15, 17, 18)? Says what stands in the way, if anything.
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day you want the answer for, usually today (YYYY-MM-DD); the grant is payable only once the transaction is completed
      `what my transaction is` IS A `Transaction kind` @desc What the grant is sought for. One of: a contract for the purchase of a home; a comprehensive home building contract (a builder builds the whole home for you); the building of a home by an owner builder; the purchase of a building to be placed on land in which the purchaser has a relevant interest (a transportable or relocated home)
      `the date my contract was made` IS A DATE @desc The date your purchase or building contract was made, or the date of the contract to buy a building you will move onto your land (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date laying the foundations began` IS A DATE @desc Owner builders only: the date laying the foundations for the home began, or another date the Commissioner has fixed as appropriate (YYYY-MM-DD; for any other transaction give the contract date again)
      `the home is in the Northern Territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home is (or will be) in the Northern Territory
      `the building is fixed to land and may lawfully be lived in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the building is affixed to land and may lawfully be used as a place of residence
      `the Commissioner considers the building suitable to live in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner considers it a suitable building for use as a place of residence (s 4(b)); answer yes unless told otherwise
      `I am or will be an owner of the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have, or on completion will have, a relevant interest in the land the home is on (see the relevant interest question)
      `the home has been lived in or sold as a residence before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home has ever been occupied or sold as a place of residence, including as a hotel room, serviced apartment or workers accommodation (answer no for a home being built for you)
      `my purchase is a taxable sale of substantially renovated new residential premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your purchase is, under the GST Act, a taxable supply of new residential premises created by substantial renovation (s 40-75(1)(b))
      `the home has been lived in or sold as a residence since it was renovated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home has been occupied or sold as a place of residence since that substantial renovation
      `the Commissioner has declared my home a new home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has declared the home a new home for your transaction (s 4A(2))
      `my contract replaces one made, or uses an option granted, before 1 October 2024` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your contract replaces an earlier contract made before 1 October 2024, or is made under an option or right granted before then (not covered here)
      `my contract was made under an option granted before 1 July 2000` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an option or right granted before 1 July 2000 applies to the contract and the Commissioner has not declared it an eligible transaction (s 13AA(1)(a)): for a purchase, you had an option to buy the home, or the seller an option to require you to buy it; for a building contract, either party had a right or option to require the other to enter into it. Almost always no. A contract made in exercise of such an option is also one made under an option granted before 1 October 2024, so answer yes to that question too
      `the price, including GST` IS A NUMBER @desc The consideration in dollars, including GST: the price, the total price of the building work, or for an owner build what the work actually cost (not your own labour); leave out rent under a lease
      `the unencumbered value of the home` IS A NUMBER @desc Only for transactions that commenced before 1 January 2015: the full value of the home in dollars, ignoring encumbrances, including GST (otherwise 0)
      `the unencumbered value of my interest in the land` IS A NUMBER @desc Only for transactions that commenced before 1 January 2015: the full value of your interest in the land in dollars, ignoring encumbrances, including GST (otherwise 0)
      `the land is wholly within the Darwin urban area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is wholly within the urban area (Darwin, Palmerston, Litchfield, Wagait, Prescribed Area A, the Darwin Waterfront Precinct); matters only from 4 Dec 2012 to before 1 Jan 2015
      `the date I become entitled to possession` IS A DATE @desc Purchases: the date you become entitled to possession of the home under the contract (usually settlement) (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `I am to get a registered title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Purchases: whether you are to obtain a registered title to the land
      `the date the steps to register my title are taken` IS A DATE @desc Purchases with a registered title: the date the necessary steps to register your title are taken (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date the home is ready to live in` IS A DATE @desc Building contracts, owner builds and relocated buildings: the date the building is ready for occupation as a place of residence on your land (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `my age on the commencement date` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years on the commencement date (the contract date, or for an owner build the foundations date)
      `the Commissioner has exempted me from the age requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has exempted you from having to be 18 (s 8(2))
      `my citizenship or visa when I apply` IS A `Citizenship or visa` @desc Your status on the day you apply. One of: an Australian citizen; the holder of a permanent visa; a New Zealand citizen who holds a special category visa; none of these
      `my earlier grant` IS AN `Earlier grant` @desc Whether you were paid a first home owner grant before, anywhere in Australia. One of: no grant was paid on an earlier application; a grant was paid on an earlier application and has not been paid back with any penalty and interest; a grant was paid on an earlier application and was paid back with any penalty and interest; a grant was paid on an earlier application for a home used as a residence, on a transaction over the threshold amount
      `I could have got a grant before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you could have successfully applied for a first home owner grant for an earlier purchase or build you were a party to
      `I have unpaid duty from a first home owner discount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you got the NT stamp duty first home owner discount (Stamp Duty Act s 89AA) on an earlier purchase and the duty it saved has not been paid
      `my earlier residential property` IS AN `Earlier residential property` @desc Your past ownership of homes anywhere in Australia, the first that applies. One of: never held a relevant interest in residential property in Australia; held a relevant interest in residential property in Australia before 1 July 2000; held one from 1 July 2000, before the commencement date, in property used as a residence of the person or their spouse or de facto partner; held one from 1 July 2000 only in property that was the subject of an earlier application whose grant was repaid, or was not paid for want of an age exemption; held one from 1 July 2000 only in property that neither the person nor their spouse or de facto partner used as a residence
      `I will live in the home as required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you will live in the home as your principal place of residence, moving in within 12 months of completion and staying for the required period
      `the Commissioner has exempted me from living in the home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has exempted you from the residence requirement for special reasons (s 12(3)(b))
      `my relationship on the commencement date` IS A `Relationship at the commencement date` @desc Your relationship on the commencement date. One of: no spouse or de facto partner, married, a de facto partner
      `the Commissioner is satisfied we live apart for good` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Married applicants only: whether the Commissioner is satisfied that you and your husband or wife are not living together and have no intention of living together again
      `my spouse or de facto partner is applying with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse or de facto partner is a joint applicant (they must be if they will own any part of the home, s 15)
      `my partner's age on the commencement date` IS A NUMBER @desc Your spouse's or de facto partner's age in whole years on the commencement date (only if applying with you)
      `the Commissioner has exempted my partner from the age requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has exempted your spouse or de facto partner from having to be 18 (only if applying with you)
      `my partner's citizenship or visa when we apply` IS A `Citizenship or visa` @desc Your spouse's or de facto partner's status on the day you apply (only if applying with you); same choices as for you
      `my partner's earlier grant` IS AN `Earlier grant` @desc Whether your spouse or de facto partner was paid a first home owner grant before, anywhere in Australia (same choices as for you)
      `my partner could have got a grant before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse or de facto partner could have successfully applied for a first home owner grant for an earlier purchase or build they were a party to
      `my partner has unpaid duty from a first home owner discount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse or de facto partner got the NT first home owner duty discount on an earlier purchase and the duty it saved has not been paid
      `my partner's earlier residential property` IS AN `Earlier residential property` @desc Your spouse's or de facto partner's past ownership of homes anywhere in Australia (same choices as for you)
      `my partner will live in the home as required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse or de facto partner will live in the home as their principal place of residence as required (only if applying with you)
      `the Commissioner has exempted my partner from living in the home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has exempted your spouse or de facto partner from the residence requirement (only if applying with you)
      `every owner who must apply is applying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether everyone who is, or on completion will be, an owner of the home is on the application, apart from those the Regulations exclude (see the question about another owner joining)
      `someone besides me and my partner is applying with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anyone other than you and your spouse or de facto partner is on the application; their facts are not asked here
GIVETH A `Payability answer`
DECIDE `Is the first home owner grant payable to me` IS
    IF `someone besides me and my partner is applying with me`
    THEN `payability is not covered` `an applicant whose facts are not given`
    ELSE `whether the grant is payable (ss 7, 15, 17)` `the day I am asking about`
            (`my transaction from my answers` `what my transaction is` `the date my contract was made` `the date laying the foundations began` `the home is in the Northern Territory` `the building is fixed to land and may lawfully be lived in` `the Commissioner considers the building suitable to live in` `I am or will be an owner of the land` `the home has been lived in or sold as a residence before` `my purchase is a taxable sale of substantially renovated new residential premises` `the home has been lived in or sold as a residence since it was renovated` `the Commissioner has declared my home a new home` `my contract replaces one made, or uses an option granted, before 1 October 2024` `my contract was made under an option granted before 1 July 2000` `the price, including GST` `the unencumbered value of the home` `the unencumbered value of my interest in the land` `the land is wholly within the Darwin urban area`)
            (`my completion facts` `the date I become entitled to possession` `I am to get a registered title` `the date the steps to register my title are taken` `the date the home is ready to live in`)
            (`the applicants from my answers` `my age on the commencement date` `the Commissioner has exempted me from the age requirement` `my citizenship or visa when I apply` `my earlier grant` `I could have got a grant before` `I have unpaid duty from a first home owner discount` `my earlier residential property` `I will live in the home as required` `the Commissioner has exempted me from living in the home` `my relationship on the commencement date` `the Commissioner is satisfied we live apart for good` `my spouse or de facto partner is applying with me` `my partner's age on the commencement date` `the Commissioner has exempted my partner from the age requirement` `my partner's citizenship or visa when we apply` `my partner's earlier grant` `my partner could have got a grant before` `my partner has unpaid duty from a first home owner discount` `my partner's earlier residential property` `my partner will live in the home as required` `the Commissioner has exempted my partner from living in the home`)
            `every owner who must apply is applying`

§§ `s 14 -- when to apply`

@export By what date must I apply for the NT first home owner grant (s 14(5))? The application period ends 12 months after completion; the Commissioner may allow a late application (s 14(6)).
GIVEN `what my transaction is` IS A `Transaction kind` @desc What the grant is sought for. One of: a contract for the purchase of a home; a comprehensive home building contract; the building of a home by an owner builder; the purchase of a building to be placed on land in which the purchaser has a relevant interest
      `the date I become entitled to possession` IS A DATE @desc Purchases: the date you become entitled to possession of the home under the contract (usually settlement) (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `I am to get a registered title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Purchases: whether you are to obtain a registered title to the land
      `the date the steps to register my title are taken` IS A DATE @desc Purchases with a registered title: the date the necessary steps to register your title are taken (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date the home is ready to live in` IS A DATE @desc Building contracts, owner builds and relocated buildings: the date the building is ready for occupation as a place of residence on your land (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must I apply for the grant` IS
    `the end of the application period (s 14(5)(b))`
        (`the completion date (s 13(6))` `what my transaction is` (`my completion facts` `the date I become entitled to possession` `I am to get a registered title` `the date the steps to register my title are taken` `the date the home is ready to live in`))

@export Can I apply for the NT first home owner grant on this day, or only with the Commissioner's permission (s 14(5), (6))? The application period runs from the commencement date to 12 months after completion.
GIVEN `the day I want to apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you want to apply (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `what my transaction is` IS A `Transaction kind` @desc What the grant is sought for. One of: a contract for the purchase of a home; a comprehensive home building contract; the building of a home by an owner builder; the purchase of a building to be placed on land in which the purchaser has a relevant interest
      `the date my contract was made` IS A DATE @desc The date your purchase or building contract was made, or the date of the contract to buy a building you will move onto your land (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date laying the foundations began` IS A DATE @desc Owner builders only: the date laying the foundations began, or another date the Commissioner has fixed (YYYY-MM-DD; otherwise give the contract date again)
      `the date I become entitled to possession` IS A DATE @desc Purchases: the date you become entitled to possession of the home under the contract (usually settlement) (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `I am to get a registered title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Purchases: whether you are to obtain a registered title to the land
      `the date the steps to register my title are taken` IS A DATE @desc Purchases with a registered title: the date the necessary steps to register your title are taken (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date the home is ready to live in` IS A DATE @desc Building contracts, owner builds and relocated buildings: the date the building is ready for occupation as a place of residence on your land (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH AN `Application timing answer`
DECIDE `Can I apply for the grant on this day` IS
    `whether an application may be made on the day (s 14(5), (6))` `the day I want to apply` `commencement`
        (`the completion date (s 13(6))` `what my transaction is` (`my completion facts` `the date I become entitled to possession` `I am to get a registered title` `the date the steps to register my title are taken` `the date the home is ready to live in`))
    WHERE
        -- Only the kind and the two dates are read to find the commencement date; the other fields are placeholders.
        `commencement` MEANS `the commencement date (s 13(5))` (`my transaction from my answers` `what my transaction is` `the date my contract was made` `the date laying the foundations began` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 FALSE)

§§ `s 12 -- moving in and living in the home`

@export By what date must I start living in the home as my principal place of residence for the NT first home owner grant (s 12(2)(a))? Within 12 months after completion, unless the Commissioner approves longer.
GIVEN `what my transaction is` IS A `Transaction kind` @desc What the grant is sought for. One of: a contract for the purchase of a home; a comprehensive home building contract; the building of a home by an owner builder; the purchase of a building to be placed on land in which the purchaser has a relevant interest
      `the date I become entitled to possession` IS A DATE @desc Purchases: the date you become entitled to possession of the home under the contract (usually settlement) (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `I am to get a registered title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Purchases: whether you are to obtain a registered title to the land
      `the date the steps to register my title are taken` IS A DATE @desc Purchases with a registered title: the date the necessary steps to register your title are taken (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date the home is ready to live in` IS A DATE @desc Building contracts, owner builds and relocated buildings: the date the building is ready for occupation as a place of residence on your land (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the Commissioner has approved a later date for me to move in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has approved a longer period for you to start living in the home, for special reasons (s 12(3)(a)(i))
      `the end of the longer period approved` IS A DATE @desc If so, the date the longer period ends (YYYY-MM-DD; otherwise any date)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must I move into the home` IS
    `the date by which occupation must start (s 12(2)(a))`
        (`the completion date (s 13(6))` `what my transaction is` (`my completion facts` `the date I become entitled to possession` `I am to get a registered title` `the date the steps to register my title are taken` `the date the home is ready to live in`))
        `the Commissioner has approved a later date for me to move in`
        `the end of the longer period approved`

@export For how many continuous months must I live in the home for the NT first home owner grant (s 12(2)(b))? 12 months if the commencement date is from 1 Oct 2024 to before 1 Oct 2027, otherwise 6, unless the Commissioner approves a shorter period.
GIVEN `what my transaction is` IS A `Transaction kind` @desc What the grant is sought for. One of: a contract for the purchase of a home; a comprehensive home building contract; the building of a home by an owner builder; the purchase of a building to be placed on land in which the purchaser has a relevant interest
      `the date my contract was made` IS A DATE @desc The date your purchase or building contract was made, or the date of the contract to buy a building you will move onto your land (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date laying the foundations began` IS A DATE @desc Owner builders only: the date laying the foundations began, or another date the Commissioner has fixed (YYYY-MM-DD; otherwise give the contract date again)
      `the Commissioner has approved a shorter period for me to live there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has approved a shorter period of residence for special reasons (s 12(3)(a)(ii))
      `the shorter period in months` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, the shorter period approved, in months (otherwise 0)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `For how many months must I live in the home` IS
    `the months of continuous occupation required (s 12(2)(b))` `commencement` `the Commissioner has approved a shorter period for me to live there` `the shorter period in months`
    WHERE
        -- Only the kind and the two dates are read to find the commencement date; the other fields are placeholders.
        `commencement` MEANS `the commencement date (s 13(5))` (`my transaction from my answers` `what my transaction is` `the date my contract was made` `the date laying the foundations began` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 FALSE)

@export Until what date must I keep living in the home, without a break, for the NT first home owner grant (s 12(2)(b))?
GIVEN `what my transaction is` IS A `Transaction kind` @desc What the grant is sought for. One of: a contract for the purchase of a home; a comprehensive home building contract; the building of a home by an owner builder; the purchase of a building to be placed on land in which the purchaser has a relevant interest
      `the date my contract was made` IS A DATE @desc The date your purchase or building contract was made, or the date of the contract to buy a building you will move onto your land (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date laying the foundations began` IS A DATE @desc Owner builders only: the date laying the foundations began, or another date the Commissioner has fixed (YYYY-MM-DD; otherwise give the contract date again)
      `the date I moved in` IS A DATE @desc The date you started (or will start) living in the home as your principal place of residence (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the Commissioner has approved a shorter period for me to live there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has approved a shorter period of residence for special reasons (s 12(3)(a)(ii))
      `the shorter period in months` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, the shorter period approved, in months (otherwise 0)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Until what date must I keep living in the home` IS
    `the date until which occupation must continue (s 12(2)(b))` `the date I moved in`
        (`For how many months must I live in the home` `what my transaction is` `the date my contract was made` `the date laying the foundations began` `the Commissioner has approved a shorter period for me to live there` `the shorter period in months`)

§§ `s 41 -- repaying the grant (only if you were paid the grant and something has gone wrong)`

@export By what date must I tell the Commissioner in writing and repay the NT first home owner grant (s 41(2), (2A))? Thirty days from the day the law fixes for what went wrong; missing it is an offence, and interest and a penalty can follow.
GIVEN `what went wrong` IS A `Repayment trigger` @desc Why the grant must be repaid. One of: not entitled to the grant under s 7 (s 41(1)(a)); paid before completion, and on completion the consideration takes it over the threshold (s 41(1)(b)); paid in anticipation of the residence requirements, which are not complied with (s 41(1)(c)); a condition imposed under s 5(5) or s 20 is breached (s 41(1)(d)); an overpayment (s 41(1)(e))
      `the date the grant was paid to me` IS A DATE @desc The date the grant was paid (YYYY-MM-DD); used if you were not entitled to it
      `the date my transaction was completed` IS A DATE @desc The completion date (YYYY-MM-DD); used if the grant was paid before completion
      `the date by which I was to have moved in` IS A DATE @desc The date by which you had to start living in the home (see the move-in question) (YYYY-MM-DD); used for the residence requirements
      `the date it first became apparent` IS A DATE @desc The date it first became apparent that the transaction would not be eligible, or that the residence requirements would not be met (YYYY-MM-DD); used for those two cases
      `the date of the breach or overpayment` IS A DATE @desc The date the condition was breached or the overpayment occurred (YYYY-MM-DD); used for those two cases
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must I tell the Commissioner and repay the grant` IS
    `the required time (s 41(2A))` `what went wrong`
        (`Repayment dates` WITH
            `the date the grant was paid`                                IS `the date the grant was paid to me`
            `the date of completion`                                     IS `the date my transaction was completed`
            `the date by which the person was to have occupied the home` IS `the date by which I was to have moved in`
            `the date it first became apparent`                          IS `the date it first became apparent`
            `the date the breach or overpayment occurred`                IS `the date of the breach or overpayment`)

@export How much interest do I owe on a repayment of the NT first home owner grant I have not made on time (s 41(3)(a), (12))? At the statutory interest rate: the market rate plus 8%.
GIVEN `the amount I have not repaid` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the grant or overpayment not repaid by the required time, in dollars
      `the date it fell due` IS A DATE @desc The required time: the last day for repaying (see the repayment question) (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date I pay it` IS A DATE @desc The date it is (or will be) paid (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the market interest rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The market interest rate for the financial year under the Taxation Administration Act s 35(2), as a decimal (0.0435 for 4.35%); the prescribed rate, or the RBA's average 90-day bank accepted bill yield for the May before
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much interest do I owe on a late repayment` IS
    `the interest on the amount in default (s 41(3)(a), (12))` `the amount I have not repaid` `the market interest rate` (`days from` `the date it fell due` `the date I pay it`)

@export If the Commissioner sends me a notice about an unpaid repayment of the NT first home owner grant, how much can it require me to pay within 30 days (s 41(3)(b), (7))? The amount, the interest, and a penalty equal to the amount, less anything remitted.
GIVEN `the amount I have not repaid` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the grant or overpayment in default, in dollars
      `the interest so far` IS A NUMBER @desc The interest accrued on it (see the interest question), in dollars
      `the penalty and interest the Commissioner has remitted` IS A NUMBER @desc Any part of the penalty or interest the Commissioner has remitted (s 41(7)), in dollars (otherwise 0)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What can the Commissioner's notice require me to pay` IS
    `what the Commissioner's notice can require (s 41(3)(b), (7))` `the amount I have not repaid` `the interest so far` `the penalty and interest the Commissioner has remitted`

@export Is what I owe under s 41 a charge on my home, so that it binds my interest in the home (s 41(5))?
GIVEN `I owe an amount under s 41` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are liable to repay the grant, an overpayment, interest or a penalty under s 41
      `I have an interest in the home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have an interest in the home for which the grant was paid
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I owe a charge on my home` IS
    `the liability is an overriding statutory charge on the person's interest in the home (s 41(5))` `I owe an amount under s 41` `I have an interest in the home`

@export We applied together: can I be made to repay all of the NT first home owner grant, not just my share (s 41(11))?
GIVEN `how many of us applied` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people were on the application on which the grant was paid
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be made to repay all of it` IS
    `the liability is joint and several (s 41(11))` `how many of us applied`

§§ `s 21 -- if an applicant dies before the application is decided`

@export What happens to our NT first home owner grant application if an applicant dies before it is decided (s 21)?
GIVEN `another applicant survives` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died was one of 2 or more applicants and at least one of the others is alive
      `they had not moved in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died had not yet lived in the home as their principal place of residence
      `the Commissioner is satisfied they meant to live there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied that the person who died intended to meet the residence requirements
GIVETH A `Death answer`
DECIDE `What happens to our application if an applicant dies` IS
    `what happens to the application on an applicant's death (s 21)` `another applicant survives` `they had not moved in` `the Commissioner is satisfied they meant to live there`
